      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The number of bariatric (weight loss) surgeries have increased steadily in the past decade. Along with the tangible benefit of this treatment, there is a risk for postoperative complications, the main cause of which is impaired absorption of nutrients. The paper describes polyradiculoneuropathy running as a type of Guillain-Barré syndrome."},
